WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.000
Speaker 1: There are only so many major news
stories each year, and we have one of them

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.000
today.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.700
And this is actually, I would argue, one of
the biggest news stories of the decade.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:16.010
We've been waiting for the Supreme Court's
decision on abortion rights to cases that

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:22.410
historically establish the right to an abortion
in most cases in the United States.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.460
Those are Roe v Wade and Planned Parenthood.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:31.340
V Casey, the Supreme Court, we knew sometime
in the next few weeks, maybe by the end of

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:38.270
June, would issue a decision on a mississippi
abortion ban which would in practice overturn

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.530
Roe v Wade and Planned Parenthood v Casey.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:46.399
Depending on what the court decides and that
decision has been leaked, it has not been

00:00:46.399 --> 00:00:50.360
announced by the Supreme Court, but it has
been leaked and reputable.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:01:00.680
So and if nothing changes, the Supreme Court
will be overturning abortion rights as a federal

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.270
in most cases.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:03.270
Right.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:08.659
Sending it back to the states, plunging many
states back into.

00:01:08.659 --> 00:01:10.159
Should we call it medieval times?

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:11.639
Should we call it the dark ages?

00:01:11.639 --> 00:01:13.049
Should we call it the 1850s?

00:01:13.049 --> 00:01:14.710
The 1950s?

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:16.340
There are actually two cases here.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:21.470
Most people know about Roe v Wade, but there's
two cases, Roe v Wade, as well as the 1992

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.990
Planned Parenthood decision.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:25.029
Supreme Court decision.

00:01:25.029 --> 00:01:26.609
Planned Parenthood v Casey.

00:01:26.609 --> 00:01:29.590
Now, Politico got a copy of the draft opinion.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.700
And this is this is a major scoop.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:32.700
It really is.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.399
And there are conservatives mad about the
fact that this leaked but obtaining this is

00:01:36.399 --> 00:01:45.840
a major scoop and the quote from the majority
opinion believed to be ready to go in a few

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:53.450
weeks is from Supreme Court Justice Samuel
Alito, where he writes, quote, Roe was egregiously

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:55.740
wrong from the start.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:02:01.200
Its reasoning was exceptionally weak, and
the decision has had damaging consequences.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.450
And far from bringing about a national settlement
of the abortion issue, Roe and Casey have

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.619
inflamed debate and deepened division.

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:14.250
Now, before we go forward with the analysis
on the assumption that this decision isn't

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:19.939
going to change, we should put on record in
case things do change, that sometimes justices

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:26.469
will circulate draft opinions and there's
still revisions and changes and sometimes

00:02:26.469 --> 00:02:27.930
horse trading for votes.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:28.930
I mean, things happen.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:32.180
You would think that that doesn't happen at
the Supreme Court, but it does.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:36.130
And up until days before it's made official.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:40.870
Opinions can change, but right now, Roe v
Wade goes bye bye.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:44.680
Planned Parenthood v Casey goes Bye bye now.

